<div id="2026-09-10-invoice-auto-create-supplier" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — Invoice entry auto-creates missing suppliers</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> When a user enters an invoice from Chat-with-AI and the supplier doesn't exist in the system, the AI now auto-creates the supplier from the parsed party name instead of failing and telling the user to go to /Inventory manually.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Previously, pasting an invoice from a supplier not already in the DB (e.g. OpenRouter, Inc) returned "No supplier matches — go to /Inventory" which broke the workflow and required a manual round-trip. Now the supplier is created inline and the draft invoice proceeds immediately.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How.</strong> Added _auto_create_supplier and _web_lookup_supplier to Model::AI2::InvoiceCreate. The web lookup queries DuckDuckGo for supplier contact info (email, phone) and populates the supplier row. Duplicate suppliers are detected before creation. Unique constraints added to inventory_supplier_invoices and inventory_customer_invoices on (sitename, invoice_number) to prevent re-entry.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/InvoiceCreate.pm</code> — added <code>_auto_create_supplier</code>, <code>_web_lookup_supplier</code>, duplicate check; modified <code>create_from_params</code> to auto-create suppliers. <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Accounting/InventorySupplierInvoice.pm</code> and <code>InventoryCustomerInvoice.pm</code> — added unique_constraint on (sitename, invoice_number).</p>
</div>
